  "jobTitle": "Software Developer",
  "summary": "I’m a software and data engineer who turns fragmented enterprise data and manual workflows into reliable production systems. My strongest work sits at the intersection of data engineering, enterprise integration, automation, and operational problem-solving.\n\nDuring more than four years as a Software Engineer in General Motors Legal IT, I designed, developed, deployed, and supported production pipelines and integrations for legal, compliance, warranty, analytics, and operations teams. I owned the complete lifecycle of six production data pipelines and provided support for 12 additional pipelines. I also migrated eight production pipelines to Databricks and supported more than 30 Power BI dashboards and reports.\nMy technical experience includes Python, SQL, PySpark, Apache Spark, Databricks, REST APIs, Microsoft Graph API, Power BI, Git, CI/CD, workflow scheduling, secure transfers, data validation, reconciliation, and production troubleshooting.\n\nOne project involved building the first automated daily regulatory workflow integrating legal, warranty, and vehicle data. The solution validated and standardized the results, securely delivered outputs to an external partner, and eliminated more than 90 hours of manual processing annually. In another project, I refactored an inherited PySpark matching workflow by removing unnecessary intermediate DataFrames and joins, reducing its runtime to approximately eight minutes and making it practical for production use.\n\nMy work has required close collaboration with people from different technical and business backgrounds. I’m comfortable translating business needs into technical requirements, explaining constraints clearly, and resolving cross-system dependencies. I get along with people easily, have consistently received strong performance reviews, and adapt quickly when a project requires an unfamiliar technology, toolset, or way of working.\n\nI’m also continuing to expand my experience with AI-enabled engineering. I use tools such as GitHub Copilot, Codex, ChatGPT, and Databricks Genie Code to support development, debugging, refactoring, and documentation while independently reviewing and validating the results. I have also built a personal context-aware LLM workflow prototype using targeted context retrieval, prompt orchestration, structured outputs, and summarization.\nI’m particularly interested in data engineering, software engineering, enterprise integration, automation, and the dependable data foundations required for AI-enabled systems.",
